Problem Statement
1.	Create an interface named Greeting with a single method sayHello().
2.	Create another class, e.g., GreetingDemo, containing a method generateGreeting().
3.	Inside generateGreeting(), implement the Greeting interface using an anonymous inner class.
4.	Print a greeting message (e.g., “Hello! Welcome to Java Programming.”).
5.	In the main() method, call generateGreeting() to execute the anonymous class behavior.
Requirements
•	Use an interface with one method (sayHello()).
•	Implement that interface using an anonymous inner class.
•	Call the implemented method within generateGreeting().
•	No separate class should explicitly implement the interface.
